<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Catholicon (Breton dictionary)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1464</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Catholicon is a Breton–French–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> dictionary compiled in 1464 by Jehan Lagadeuc, a cleric of the diocese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treguier">Tréguier</a>, and printed at Tréguier in 1499. It is the first dictionary of the Breton language and one of the earliest dictionaries to include French, and it is a key source for Middle Breton.</p></div>
